# DLLs too large to commit.
#
# GitHub rejects any pushed file over 100 MiB. nvngx_dlssnr.dll (DLSS 5 Neural
# Rendering) is ~158 MiB, so it ships as a release asset instead and the client
# finds it through the "url" key on its manifest.json entry.
#
# Git LFS is not an option: raw.githubusercontent.com serves the LFS pointer
# text rather than the binary, which the client would cache as the DLL.
#
# Keep the file in dlls/ locally so it sits alongside the others - just never
# commit it. To publish a new build:
#   gh release create nvngx_dlssnr-<version> dlls/nvngx_dlssnr.dll \
#     --repo Recol/DLSS-Updater-DLLs --title "nvngx_dlssnr.dll <version>"
# then update both "version" and "url" in manifest.json.
dlls/nvngx_dlssnr.dll
